enus globals: hyphen-chain and money fields (Mudb0y 2467160+a25d0ee6)

Ports the language declarations both rule sets need, in dependency
order: hyphen_chain_next (one long: where the number after a hyphen
begins in a chain of them) then the seven money shorts (a thirteenth
currency kind plus six dollar kinds). Counts 800->808, state bytes
0x10a0->0x10c4 (+36: 8+28), so the u_vars stores at 4260+ land
inside the machine. No behaviour change alone: no rule names the
new fields until the et_numbr.up port arrives with them.

diff --git a/lang/enus/delta_globals_enus.c b/lang/enus/delta_globals_enus.c
index 6f57118..938d7ff 100644
--- a/lang/enus/delta_globals_enus.c
+++ b/lang/enus/delta_globals_enus.c
@@ -145,10 +145,11 @@ const int8_t enus_delta_globals[] = {
     DG_SHORT, DG_SHORT, DG_SHORT, DG_SHORT, DG_SHORT, DG_SHORT,
     DG_SHORT, DG_SHORT, DG_SHORT, DG_SHORT, DG_SHORT, DG_WORD,
     DG_LONG, DG_WORD, DG_SHORT, DG_SHORT, DG_SHORT, DG_SHORT,
-    DG_SHORT, DG_SHORT,
+    DG_SHORT, DG_SHORT, DG_LONG, DG_SHORT, DG_SHORT, DG_SHORT,
+    DG_SHORT, DG_SHORT, DG_SHORT, DG_SHORT,
 };
 
-const int32_t enus_delta_globals_n = 800;
+const int32_t enus_delta_globals_n = 808;
 
 /* What the compound ones hold, in the same order they appear
    in the list above. */
@@ -181,4 +182,4 @@ const int32_t enus_delta_compounds_n = 20;
    machine of this language has to be. The struct in delta.h
    stops at the named fields; the cells are the rest of an
    allocation this size. */
-const int32_t enus_delta_state_bytes = 0x10a0;
+const int32_t enus_delta_state_bytes = 0x10c4;
diff --git a/lang/enus/enus.globals b/lang/enus/enus.globals
index 75dc854..9f50208 100644
--- a/lang/enus/enus.globals
+++ b/lang/enus/enus.globals
@@ -112,3 +112,16 @@ word 1
 # which set_global_constants sets to two and one; and whether a slash was
 # read as per, with the one it is compared against.
 short 6
+
+# One of ours: where the number after a hyphen begins when that hyphen is one
+# of a chain of them, so that the hyphen after that number is read as one of
+# the chain too. hyphen_in_chain in et_numbr.up sets it and reset_sent_vars
+# clears it.
+long 1
+name long 39 hyphen_chain_next
+
+# Seven that 6.1 declares and 4.3 never had, which its money rules lifted into
+# et_numbr.up compare against: a thirteenth kind of currency, where both number
+# the first eleven alike, and six kinds of dollar. set_global_constants sets
+# them to 6.1's values.
+short 7
